# GhettoRack on a Pi: the HDMI ports' remote-control (CEC) devices are tagged as
# pointing sticks, so the kiosk's compositor thinks a mouse is there and draws an
# arrow that never goes away. libinput (the compositor) leaves them alone; the
# bridge reads the TV remote from the device itself and is not affected.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="vc4-hdmi-*", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
